// Atepomaros's cousins, keeping the pen. One of them can be paid to look the
// other way after dark.
=== start
[flag lit_gone] -> empty
[flag lit_free] -> empty
"Atepomaros says nobody goes near the pen." He shifts the spear, not quite at you.
* [!flag kin_bribed, silver 20] "Cold work. Here's twenty for something to drink, after dark, a long way from the gate." -> bribe ~ silver -20
* [flag kin_bribed] "Remember: after dark, a long way from the gate." -> reminded
* "What's she to you?" -> what
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== bribe
~ set kin_bribed
He looks at the silver, then at the house, and then he takes it and puts it away fast. "There's a jar at the miller's," he says, to nobody. "I'll be there tonight. Late."
* Go. -> END

=== reminded
"I heard you." He doesn't look at you.
* Go. -> END

=== what
"Nothing. A Roman's woman." He shrugs. "He's my cousin. If he says watch a pen, I watch a pen."
* Go. -> END

=== empty
"Nothing to keep now." He leans the spear on the wall and looks at the straw.
* Go. -> END
